WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.100
Kevin Feige, who has served as the president
of Marvel Studios since before the MCU was

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.360
even a thing, finally broke his silence about
the future of Marvel fans' favorite armored

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:10.320
hero.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:14.800
Recently, he shed just the teensiest bit of
light on who might replace Iron Man in the

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:19.280
MCU, who notably sacrificed his life for the
safety of the entire universe in Avengers:

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:20.160
Endgame.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:23.400
Turns out we won't be seeing a replacement
for quite some time.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:27.980
Past reports have focused on the Marvel Comics
character Ironheart: a girl named Riri Williams

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:32.320
who builds her own superhero suit based on
Iron Man's armor and even gets his stamp of

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:37.090
approval to be a vigilante, would be the lucky
one to assume the Iron Man mantle in the wake

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:38.410
of Tony Stark's death.

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:43.110
After Iron Man falls into a coma following
a fight in a comic storyline, Riri protects

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:47.000
innocent civilians in his stead, looking out
for the world as Ironheart.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.880
It makes sense that Ironheart might replace
Iron Man on the big screen given her personal

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:55.740
evolution in the comics, but Feige hinted
that it isn't a done deal in the slightest.

00:00:55.740 --> 00:01:01.000
In an interview with BET ahead of the July
2 release of Spider-Man: Far From Home, Feige

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:05.580
got to talking about a replacement for Iron
Man when the interviewer, Jerry L. Barrow,

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:10.220
mentioned that Downey Jr. had said during
the Gene Siskel Film Center Gala in June that

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:12.340
Ironheart should join the MCU.

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:16.520
Feige shared that he adores the character
of Riri Williams, but admitted that nothing

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:18.320
is set in stone at this time.

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:19.380
Feige told Barrow:

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:30.460
Without using words, Feige essentially clarified
that he doesn't know what the future holds

00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:35.500
for Ironheart and isn't at liberty to discuss
whether or not she can, will, or should be

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:36.800
a part of the MCU.

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:40.960
Later on in the interview, Feige mentioned
that he continues to be blown away by fans'

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:45.370
response to Marvel Comics characters, and
fully understands why there's a seemingly

00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:49.160
never-ending list of heroes people want to
see debut in the MCU.

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:53.259
He owned up to initially finding the constant
questions about whether particular characters

00:01:53.259 --> 00:01:57.659
would appear on the big screen to be frustrating,
then said that he now views it as a great

00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:00.640
privilege to be able to make movies for such
a passionate fandom.

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:04.780
Fans have long thought Riri Williams would
eventually suit up as Ironheart and fly into

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:08.789
the MCU, and the desire to see that happen
has only burned stronger in the time since

00:02:08.789 --> 00:02:11.620
Avengers: Endgame debuted in theaters in late
April.

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:16.480
The final moments of the film saw Iron Man
snap his fingers, turn Thanos and his alien

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:21.090
army to dust, and die knowing that his passing
meant a safe future for his family and his

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:22.200
fellow Avengers.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:26.640
When another Avenger, Chris Evans' Captain
America, passed on his superhero mantle to

00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:32.090
Anthony Mackie's Sam Wilson, many Marvelites
wondered how the MCU would fill the Iron Man-sized

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:34.500
gap and who would be the hero to replace him.

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:35.980
"I'll be Tony Stark."

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:36.560
"What?"

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:40.980
Sorry Brucie…the general consensus is that
Ironheart should be that vigilante - and it

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:42.849
isn't just fans who support the idea.

00:02:42.849 --> 00:02:47.280
Robert Downey Jr. clearly does, and Spider-Man
actor Tom Holland does as well.

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:51.520
Previously asked about who he would like to
see join the MCU down the line, Holland answered,

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:52.380
quote:

00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:05.480
Even still, Feige's comments to BET make sense.

00:03:05.489 --> 00:03:09.910
It really is too early to say when and if
Ironheart will soar into the Marvel movie

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:14.459
universe, since the characters in the MCU
haven't yet begun to grieve the loss of Iron

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:18.280
Man...and because Marvel still hasn't announced
what's coming next in Phase 4.

